  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.659,
            0.132,
            0.86
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Curiosity | Textbook of Science| Grade 6 6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.093,
            0.884,
            0.176
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The normal temperature of a healthy human body is taken to be "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 7 . 0   ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . But in this activity, did you find that the normal temperature of every person was "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 7 . 0   ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } ?"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Or did you find the temperature slightly higher or lower for some people?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.094,
            0.21,
            0.29,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do small children generally have slightly higher body temperatures as compared to adults?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.092,
            0.354,
            0.319,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do old people, even",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " when healthy, generall "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "have lower body temperatures than young adults?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.511,
            0.382,
            0.667
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "usianve seen a friend of mine uhng a digital thermometen aat reads temperature cte he iferent scale. It shows dae hormal temperature sf a cealthy human body as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "9 8 . 6 ~ ^ { \\circ } \\tilde { F } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " What is the reason for this difference?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.67,
            0.359,
            0.862
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.207,
                0.67,
                0.359,
                0.862
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.409,
            0.176,
            0.884,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The temperature of every person may not be "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 7 . 0   ^ { \\circ } \\mathsf { C } ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " What we call normal temperature is the average body temperature of a large number of healthy people. A perfectly healthy person may, therefore, have a normal temperature slightly different from "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 7 . 0 ~ ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . The body temperature is influenced by several factors, such as age, time of the day and activity level."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.41,
            0.358,
            0.885,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You may try measuring your own temperature at different times of the day and on different days. Record the thermometer readings in your notebook. After a month, analyse your temperature record and see if there are any variations. If yes, try to think what might be the reasons for that."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.41,
            0.5,
            0.882,
            0.541
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The temperature of human beings does not normally go below "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 5 \\; ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or above "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 2 \\; ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } ,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.409,
            0.541,
            0.884,
            0.663
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For measuring the body temperature of small children or old people, the digital thermometer can also be placed in the armpit. The temperature measured this way is about "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 . 5 ~ ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 ^ { \\circ } \\mathsf { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " lower than the actual body temperature."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.409,
            0.663,
            0.885,
            0.909
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "There is another scale of temperature known as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fahrenheit scale",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". On this scale, the unit of temperature is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "degreeFahrenheit",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and is denoted by °F. A temperature measured as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 7 . 0   ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " on Celsius scale is equivalent to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "9 8 . 6   ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { F }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " on Fahrenheit scale. The Fahrenheit scale is not used in most scientific studies anymore. In scientific work, there is another scale of temperature known as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Kelvin scale",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". On this scale, the unit for temperature is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "kelvin",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and is denoted by K. The "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "SI unit of temperature",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is kelvin."
            }
          ]
        },
